claim.claim-text:
storage circuitry configured to store node data for a spatially organized acceleration data structure, including to store the following node information for a given node:
origin coordinates for the node; and
for a given child node of multiple child nodes, child information that includes:
quantized bounding region information for a bounding region corresponding to the child node, wherein the quantized bounding region information encodes bounding region coordinates as offsets relative to the origin coordinates;

the bounding regions corresponding to the child nodes are box-shaped bounding regions;
the quantized bounding information indicates two opposite corners of a given box-shaped bounding region; and
the quantized bounding region information is quantized using rounding out for the two opposite corners.

determine bounds represented by the quantized bounding region information;
generate a reciprocal of a given ray;
order intersection results.

storing, by a computing system, node data for a spatially organized acceleration data structure, including the following node information for a given node:
origin coordinates for the node; and
for a given child node of multiple child nodes, child information that includes:
quantized bounding region information for a bounding region corresponding to the child node, wherein the quantized bounding region information encodes bounding region coordinates as offsets relative to the origin coordinates;

origin coordinates for the node; and
for a given child node of multiple child nodes, child information that includes:
quantized bounding region information for a bounding region corresponding to the child node, wherein the quantized bounding region information encodes bounding region coordinates as offsets relative to the origin coordinates.

the bounding regions corresponding to the child nodes are box-shaped bounding regions;
the quantized bounding information indicates two opposite corners of a given box-shaped bounding region; and
the quantized bounding region information is quantized using rounding out for the two opposite corners.
